 "_about": [
  "Episode 3 cues: what happens on screen in each beat, step by step, keyed by the beat IDs of ep3/outline.json and ep3/script.fountain.",
  "Step forms as in ep1/cues.json.  A visual may carry 'delay' (seconds after its step starts) and 'phase' (which part of a multi-step visual plays now).",
  "Everything is drawn from build_math_objects.py's MINIMOG, tetracode and odd-man-out test (through cue_tools.Code), never from values typed here.  Values written in a cue ('rows', 'word', 'counts', 'readings', 'at', 'fix', 'repairs', 'totals', ...) are claims: check_outline.py recomputes each one and stops on a mismatch.",
  "'board': 'minimog' plays the MINIMOG verbs through cue_tools.Code.  The grid stays up all episode on the left, with its row numbers and a reading slot under each column; the clock, the codewords and the counts sit on the right."
 ],
